---
/** Privacy policy body in English. Section titles come from src/i18n → privacy.toc. */
import LegalSection from "@/components/legal/LegalSection.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "@/data/company";
import { SITE } from "@/data/site";
import { i18n, type Dictionary } from "@/i18n";

interface Props {
  toc: Dictionary["privacy"]["toc"];
}

const { toc } = Astro.props;
const { href } = i18n(Astro);
---

<LegalSection id="responsable" title={toc["responsable"]}>
  <p>
    The controller of your personal data is <strong>{SITE.legalName}</strong> ("GVolts", "we", "us"), a company that
    designs, installs and monitors fire alarm, electronic security and electrical systems.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> {CONTACT.address.join(", ")}</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a></li>
    <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref}>{CONTACT.phone}</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>For any privacy question you can write to us at the email address above.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="datos" title={toc["datos"]}>
  <p>We only collect the data we need to help you. Depending on how you interact with us:</p>
  <h3>Contact and quote form</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Full name, phone number, email address and ZIP code.</li>
    <li>The service you're interested in and the description of your project.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Newsletter subscription</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email address, if you choose to subscribe to receive promotions or news.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Live chat</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The messages you send us and, if you provide them, your name and contact details. Only enabled if you accept functional cookies.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Browsing data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Aggregate usage statistics (pages viewed, device type, approximate country) through a self-hosted analytics
      tool that doesn't use tracking cookies or allow us to identify you. Only enabled if you accept it.
    </li>
    <li>Technical data your browser sends automatically (IP address, date and time) in the server logs, for security purposes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't collect special categories of data (health, ethnic origin, political opinions, etc.) or payment details through this site.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="finalidades" title={toc["finalidades"]}>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your inquiries, schedule site visits and prepare quotes.</li>
    <li>To provide the services you've hired: installation, maintenance, inspections and monitoring.</li>
    <li>To send you marketing communications only if you've subscribed; you can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
    <li>To improve the website based on aggregate, anonymous statistics.</li>
    <li>To protect the site against fraudulent or abusive use and to meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>We don't sell or rent your personal data</strong>, and we don't use it for automated decision-making or profiling with legal effects on you.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="base-legal" title={toc["base-legal"]}>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your consent:</strong> when you submit the form, subscribe or accept optional cookies. You can withdraw it whenever you like.</li>
    <li><strong>Pre-contractual steps and performance of a contract:</strong> to prepare your quote and provide the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> to keep the site secure and improve our services, always balanced against your rights.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> to comply with tax, accounting and fire safety regulations.</li>
  </ul>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="conservacion" title={toc["conservacion"]}>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact requests that don't become clients:</strong> up to 24 months from the last contact.</li>
    <li><strong>Clients:</strong> for the duration of the contractual relationship and, afterwards, for as long as applicable laws require (usually between 5 and 7 years for tax and warranty obligations).</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter subscription:</strong> until you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li><strong>Chat conversations:</strong> up to 12 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Server technical logs:</strong> a maximum of 90 days.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Once these periods expire, we securely delete or anonymize the data.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="destinatarios" title={toc["destinatarios"]}>
  <p>We only share data with providers that help us deliver the service and that are contractually bound to protect it and use it solely on our instructions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Web hosting and database:</strong> the servers where this site runs and where requests are stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> Resend, for notifications and welcome emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Live chat:</strong> Chatwoot, only if you enable functional cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Monitoring centers and manufacturers:</strong> when you sign up for a monitoring or warranty service that requires it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may also disclose data to public authorities, fire departments or law enforcement when required by law or necessary to respond to an emergency.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="transferencias" title={toc["transferencias"]}>
  <p>
    Some of our providers may process data outside your country of residence. When that happens, we require
    appropriate safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses or equivalent certifications, so your data keeps
    the same level of protection.
  </p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="derechos" title={toc["derechos"]}>
  <p>Depending on the regulations that apply to you, you can exercise the following rights at any time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access:</strong> know what data about you we process.</li>
    <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> ask us to delete your data.</li>
    <li><strong>Objection and restriction:</strong> object to certain processing or ask us to restrict it.</li>
    <li><strong>Portability:</strong> receive your data in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent:</strong> without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Non-discrimination:</strong> you won't be treated differently for exercising your rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise them, email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}?subject=Privacy%20rights`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>
    stating your request. We may ask for additional information to verify your identity. We'll respond within 30
    days at most (45 days where the law allows it due to the complexity of the request).
  </p>
  <p>If you believe we haven't handled your request properly, you can file a complaint with the competent data protection or consumer protection authority.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="seguridad" title={toc["seguridad"]}>
  <p>
    We apply technical and organizational measures proportionate to the risk: encrypted communications (HTTPS),
    restricted access to the admin panel, strong passwords, backups and staff training. No system is infallible,
    but if we detect a breach affecting your data we'll notify you and the authorities within the timeframes
    required by law.
  </p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="clientes" title={toc["clientes"]}>
  <p>
    When we install or monitor cameras, access control or alarm systems, the images and logs those systems
    generate belong to our client. In those cases GVolts acts as a <strong>data processor</strong>: we only access
    them to provide the contracted service (support, maintenance or alarm verification), following the client's
    instructions and the signed contract. The client is responsible for informing the people being recorded and
    for complying with applicable video surveillance regulations.
  </p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="menores" title={toc["menores"]}>
  <p>This site is intended for adults. We don't knowingly collect data from children under 16. If you believe a minor has provided us with data, contact us and we'll delete it.</p>
</LegalSection>

<LegalSection id="cambios" title={toc["cambios"]}>
  <p>
    We may update this policy to reflect legal changes or changes to our services. We'll publish the current
    version on this page with its update date and, if the change is significant, we'll let you know through an
    appropriate channel. See also our <a href={href("/cookies")}>Cookie policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalSection>
